<h2 id="ai">9. Use of AI</h2>
<p>AI plays two separate roles in this project, which are kept apart:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>As the object of study</strong> (aim 3, phase 2): AI-assisted testing is one of the methods being compared. Its prompts, models and settings will be published as part of the method, and its output is classified with the same protocol as the tools.</li>
  <li><strong>As a research assistant</strong>: AI models (Anthropic Claude) draft the WCAG mapping, propose new test cases and help with code and documentation.</li>
</ul>
<p>To keep the assistant role transparent and repeatable:</p>
<ul>
  <li>AI output that affects results is stored as data, with the model, the date and a one-sentence rationale for each item.</li>
  <li>Material that no human has reviewed is marked <q>AI-drafted, not human-reviewed</q>.</li>
  <li>Results are always computed by deterministic scripts from stored data. Rerunning them does not need an AI.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="reproduce">10. How to reproduce</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Clone the <a href="{{ site.repo }}">repository</a> and check out the commit named in the run you want to reproduce.</li>
  <li>Install with Node.js 24 and npm 11.15 or later: <code>npm ci</code>.</li>
  <li>Build and verify: <code>npm run build</code>, then <code>npm run verify</code>.</li>
  <li>Recompute WCAG coverage: <code>npm run wcag:coverage</code>.</li>
  <li>Install the browser and run the retest: <code>npm run retest:browsers</code>, then <code>npm run retest</code>. Raw output and the environment record are written to <code>data/results/ail-2026/runs/&lt;runId&gt;/</code>. Details are in the <a href="{{ wiki }}method/retest-procedure.md">retest procedure</a>.</li>
  <li>Classify the raw output: <code>npm run classify</code> (or <code>node scripts/classify.mjs data/results/ail-2026/runs/&lt;runId&gt;</code>). It writes <code>classification.json</code> next to the raw output and gives byte-identical output when run again. See the <a href="{{ wiki }}method/classification-protocol.md">classification protocol</a>.</li>
</ol>
<p>Data lives in <a href="{{ tree }}data">data/</a>: WCAG source data, the mappings, the gap analysis, and results by origin (<code>govuk-2017</code>, <code>ail-2026</code>).</p>

<h2 id="limitations">11. Limitations</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Exact comparison with 2017 is limited: 2017 tool versions are unknown, and classification was manual then and scripted now.</li>
  <li>Each test case contains one deliberate barrier. Real pages combine many, and tools may behave differently there.</li>
  <li>Some GOV.UK examples depend on remote media or old browser behaviour (such as <code>&lt;blink&gt;</code>) and may no longer show their barrier. Corrected AIL versions address some of these.</li>
  <li>Several WCAG criteria cannot be represented by a single static page, such as consistency across pages, timing and authentication. These need multi-page or scripted test cases.</li>
  <li>The WCAG mapping is AI-drafted and only partly reviewed.</li>
</ul>
